<Layout title="Privacy – WebP to PNG Converter" description="How the converter handles your images, temporary browser memory, downloads, and analytics. Images are processed locally without uploads.">
  <article class="article"><a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Back to the converter</a><h1>Your files stay with you.</h1><p>This notice describes the behavior of this version of WebP to PNG Converter.</p><h2>Image processing</h2><p>Selected images are read, decoded, drawn to a canvas, and exported inside your browser. Images, original filenames, and local paths are not uploaded to a server or sent to a third-party image service.</p><p>Files and results are held temporarily in browser memory. Removing a file, clearing the queue, reloading, or closing the page discards the tool’s references to them. The tool does not use cookies, local storage, or IndexedDB to save images or conversion history.</p><h2>Downloads</h2><p>A download starts only when you choose a PNG or ZIP download action. Your browser controls the save location and may keep its own download history. Clearing this page does not delete a file you already downloaded.</p><h2>Website traffic and analytics</h2><p>No GA4, Microsoft Clarity, Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon, or other production analytics script is enabled in this version. The development server can print sanitized event counts and size or duration ranges in the browser console. It does not print filenames, images, paths, or raw errors.</p><p>Loading the website still makes ordinary requests for HTML, scripts, styles, and public guide images. A hosting provider can receive normal request information such as an IP address and browser headers. That is separate from uploading your selected images.</p><h2>Future changes</h2><p>If analytics or hosting behavior changes, this notice must be updated to describe the services actually enabled. Contact information is listed on the <a href="/about/">About page</a> when available.</p></article>
</Layout>
